        "title": "using the optimization method proposed in Ref. [19], we ﬁnd a polynomial P(x) ∈C[x] of odd degree d such that max x∈[-1,1] | Re P(x) -S(x; δ, ϵ)| ≤ϵ′, where P(x) is characterized by a sequence of phase factors {ϕj}d j=0 satisfying P(x) • • • ! = eiϕ0σz d Y j=1 [R(x)eiϕjσz], (7) where R(x) = x √ 1 -x2 √ 1 -x2 -x ! . The existence of the phase factors is guaranteed by [23, Theorem 5]. Ref. [19] uses quasi- Newton method to solve a least squares problem to obtain these phase factors, and we terminate the iteration only when L∞error of the residual of the real part is smaller than ϵ′ = 10-4",
